From: mothershipOS
Subject: [PATCH] sensors: the host streams only the active sensors

The goldfish multi-HAL enables every sensor on the host once (set:<name>:1 for the whole mask) and filters
activation inside the guest; the update interval only follows batch(). On the emulator that is free; with
mothershipOS the host is a phone whose sensor DSP then streams accelerometer, gyroscope and magnetometer at the
fastest rate ever asked for, the whole time the VM runs. Now activate() forwards set:<name>:<0|1> (the protocol
has it), the listener enables only the active sensors when it (re)connects, and the interval is recomputed from
the active streaming sensors on activation changes too (an on-change sensor's period does not count).

